; A ?: whose result is a record (or other aggregate) does not carry the value
; out of its arms with cir.yield: both arms store into a temporary and the value
; is loaded after the ternary.  The CIR-to-CIR call conversion lowering of the
; newer pins accepts a record value only in a store, a call, a return or a
; member read; a yielded record is "not yet implemented" there (corpus case
; opt/nrv5).  The program checks both arms at -O0 and -O2, in a function,
; nested, as the initializer of a namespace-scope variable (a dynamic
; initializer) and as the initializer of a static local.
; RUN: cat %S/Inputs/header08_cxx.txt %s > %t.txt
; RUN: %ecil-asm %t.txt -o %t.ecil
; RUN: %edg-cir --emit=cir %t.ecil | %FileCheck %s --implicit-check-not='cir.yield %{{[0-9]+}} : !rec_S'
; RUN: %edg-cir --emit=obj -o %t.o %t.ecil
; RUN: gcc %t.o -o %t.exe
; RUN: %t.exe
; RUN: %edg-cir -O2 --emit=obj -o %t.o2.o %t.ecil
; RUN: gcc %t.o2.o -o %t.o2.exe
; RUN: %t.o2.exe

; CHECK: cir.ternary(
; CHECK: cir.call @mk1
; CHECK-NEXT: cir.store {{.*}} : !rec_S, !cir.ptr<!rec_S>
; CHECK: cir.call @mk2
; CHECK-NEXT: cir.store {{.*}} : !rec_S, !cir.ptr<!rec_S>

